# Cache Strategy Decision

**Issue:** https://github.com/example/project/issues/42
**Decided on:** 2026-10-01T14:30:00Z

**Present:** Alice, Bob, Carol

## Decision

**Option:** [Redis Cluster](#redis-cluster)

**Rationale:** Best balance of performance and flexibility for our use case

## Requirements

| Requirement | Hard | Checked |
|---|---|---|
| P99 latency under 50ms | Yes | Yes |
| Stay within infrastructure budget | Yes | Yes |
| Supports distributed tracing | No | Yes |

## Items

| Item | Answer / Value |
|---|---|
| Expected peak traffic | Over 10k RPS |
| Multi-region deployment | Single region |
| Cache TTL | 300 seconds |
| Additional notes | Prioritize simplicity over flexibility |

## Design Options

### Redis Cluster

Managed Redis with read replicas

**Status:** possible

**Requirements met:** 1/2 hard, 1/1 soft

**Effects:**
- [cost] Requires additional read replicas (changes)
- [performance] Connection pooling recommended (note)

**Pros:**
- Battle-tested
- Rich data structures

**Cons:**
- Operational overhead


### CDN Edge Cache

Cache at the edge with a CDN provider

**Status:** eliminated

**Requirements met:** 2/2 hard, 0/1 soft

**Failed requirements:** Supports distributed tracing

**Pros:**
- Zero operational overhead

**Cons:**
- Limited invalidation control

